From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: buffered animations, HitTestThemeBackground, IsCompositionActive

BeginBufferedAnimation returned NULL, so a program using soft-fade
animations (WPF/Win32 controls that call GetThemeTransitionDuration) got no
fade and had to paint the final state. It now gives the program two buffers
to paint, the initial and the final state (only the final one when the
duration is zero or the style is BPAS_NONE, as documented). EndBufferedAnimation
starts the fade: the window shows the initial state, a timer asks it to paint
every 16 ms, and BufferedPaintRenderAnimation, called from the program's
WM_PAINT, draws the frame (the initial state with the final state blended over
it, linear, cubic or sinusoidal) and returns TRUE; the last frame is the final
state and ends the animation. EndBufferedAnimation(FALSE) frees the buffers
and starts nothing; BufferedPaintStopAllAnimations and BufferedPaintUnInit
drop the fades of a window / thread. The painting parameters (exclude
rectangle, blend function) apply to every frame.

HitTestThemeBackground answered E_NOTIMPL; it tells whether the point is in
the background bounded by the rectangle, or by the region when there is one:
HTCLIENT or HTNOWHERE.

IsCompositionActive failed with ERROR_CALL_NOT_IMPLEMENTED; it asks dwmapi
(is DWM composition enabled), as the page describes.
